From 7445e77f830820f888213bd43aeb1c454c89d18a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:30:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Send the playback position the views draw, not an anchor

Core now sends each position the audio output reports on the fast stream,
one for each 8 ms of audio (one display frame at 120 Hz) and at most one per
buffer the output takes, and the macOS and Android views draw the latest
value each frame with no arithmetic. Core picks the interval instead of the
apps, which passed 200 ms. Android's output pulls 256 frames at a time so its
reports keep that pace.

Only the timeline row keeps a line, for the system media controls and
Media3. A seek always writes a new line there, so Media3 confirms its pending
seek from a line that lands within a second of the target, and the seek
count goes away. Android's seek bar seeks through core directly.

